# Zetteling Release Notes

The full, user-facing history is on the About page inside the app
(src/Zetteling/templates/about.html). Engineering notes are in DEVNOTES.md.

## 5.2.0 (November 2026)

* Note history (history.py): a copy of the file before it is overwritten,
  at most every 10 minutes while editing and always before restore, lock,
  link-mention, code rename/merge/removal and outline changes; up to 200
  per note in <app data>/history/<id>/. History page with line diff and
  restore (which saves the current version first). Locking a note encrypts
  its plain-text versions.
* Backlinks show the sentence around the link. Unlinked mentions (title or
  its main part before " — " / ": ") with one-click linking that keeps the
  source wording as [[id|text]].
* Templates (note_templates.py): .templates/ in the notes folder, seeded
  with interview memo, fieldnote, reading note, lecture plan; picker on new
  notes, palette commands, Settings → Templates (edit, new, delete,
  restore built-ins); {{date}} {{time}} {{weekday}}.
* Qualitative coding (codebook.py): [passage]{.code .code2} spans
  (pandoc bracketed spans), rendered highlighted with code chips; ⇧⌘C code
  picker; `codes` index table (unlocked notes only; locked notes read live
  while open); Codebook and code pages with definitions, categories,
  co-occurrence, rename/merge, remove, CSV export.
* Manuscripts: notes of type manuscript; ![[id]] embed lines render the
  embedded note (two levels) in any note; outline panel (move, remove, add
  note, add heading, add thread); export expands embeds.
* Search filters: kind:, tag:/-tag:, thread:, code:/-code:, after:,
  before:, is:locked/unlocked, "phrase", -word, in the search page, palette
  and link picker.
* Welcome tour: a short spotlight tour of the window (library, new
  note and templates, search, note list, edit, lock, history, export,
  side panel, writing shortcuts, browse, settings). Starts by itself once
  (settings.tour_seen, saved when it opens), again from the compass button
  in the sidebar, /tour or the palette. Skips parts not on the page;
  arrow keys, Esc, focus kept in the card; respects reduced motion.
* Help page rewritten: grouped sections, sticky contents sidebar that
  follows your place, shorter text, new features documented.
* Fixes: exports no longer pass [[id]] links to pandoc as raw brackets;
  single-note exports no longer repeat the title; notes created in the same
  second get distinct IDs.

## 5.1.0 (November 2026)

* Locked notes. Per-note lock (padlock button, palette) and per-kind lock
  (Settings → Locked notes → Always lock these kinds; existing notes of the
  kind are locked when it's ticked). Body encrypted with AES-256-GCM under a
  one-use key from HKDF-SHA-256 per save; random 256-bit data key wrapped
  under Argon2id(password) (RFC 9106 first recommended setting, falling back
  to the second) and under a 256-bit recovery key. Title, tags, kind,
  threads and dates stay plain.
* Open until quit or an idle time (5/15/30/60 min or never); "Lock now";
  inline unlock in the editor; change password; reset with recovery key;
  remove one lock or all.
* Locked text never enters the search index, links table or embeddings and
  is never sent to AI; index uses SQLite secure_delete and is optimised and
  checkpointed after locking. Export warns that output is unencrypted.
* Wrapped keys in .zetteling-vault.json in the notes folder and a copy in
  every locked note.
* Pages and API replies are sent with Cache-Control: no-store, so decrypted
  text isn't kept in the web view's disk cache.
* POSTs from other websites are refused (Origin/Referer must match), so a
  page in a browser can't drive the local server, e.g. to remove locks.

## 5.0.1 (November 2026)

* Autosave: the editor saves 1.5 s after typing stops and once more when it
  closes (pagehide beacon). Embedding runs only on that last save or on ⌘S.
  New notes are created on their first save, which waits for a title and
  for focus to leave the title field. Per-page draft token and sequence
  number: stale requests are ignored, and racing saves create one note.
  Settings → Writing → Save automatically (default on). "Cancel" reads
  "Done" when autosave is on.
* Pandoc's GPL licence and source pointer now ship inside the app; Licence
  page lists third-party components; THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.md.
* macOS requires: cryptography<49 (49+ has no Intel macOS wheels).
* Help: create/edit/delete and export instructions updated for the v5
  layout.

## 5.0.0 (November 2026)

* One-window workspace: sidebar, note list, note, side panel (thread,
  backlinks, related notes, Interrogate).
* Settings → Appearance: seven themes (four light, three dark), follow-the-Mac
  mode, accent colour, five bundled fonts, four text sizes, illustrations
  switch. Saved in settings.json.
* Command palette (⌘K) and keyboard shortcuts.
* Editor: [[ note picker and @ citation picker at the cursor; "Links in this
  note" list; unsaved-changes guard.
* Citations render as author and year (the note file keeps @citekey).
* First-run welcome screen for new installs.
* Fixes: export folder and bibliography path chosen in Settings now win over
  environment variables; Gemini defaults updated (old ones were shut down);
  retired-model warnings; HTMX and fonts bundled (no CDN, offline search);
  punctuation-safe search; duplicate renderer removed.

## 4.0.2 (April 2026)

* Replaced bibtexparser with an in-house .bib parser. See the About page.
